[{:db/id 17592186162381 :question/problem "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{100}$ is a sample of size $n=100$ drawn from a population with mean $\\mu =30$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=9,$ calculate the standard error of $\\overset{―}{X}.$" :question/worked-solution "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n},\n$$\n\nand the standard error is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]}=\\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}}.\n$$\n\nSince the population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=9$ and the sample size $n=100,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}] & =\\frac{9}{100} \\\\  & =0.09.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{0.09}=0.3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186159488 :answer-field/correct 17592186159490 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162108 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-74bfeec3-3f4e-5c4f-b7e4-18502ff50810"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-74bfeec3-3f4e-5c4f-b7e4-18502ff50810" :question/id #uuid "74bfeec3-3f4e-5c4f-b7e4-18502ff50810" :question/math-academy-id "q-143443" :question/problem "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ drawn from a population with mean $\\mu =100$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=25,$  determine the smallest sample size required so that the standard error of the mean is less than $0.25.$" :question/worked-solution "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n},\n$$\n\nand the standard error is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]}=\\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}}\n$$\n\nSince the population standard deviation is $\\sigma =\\sqrt{25}=5,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{n}}.\n$$\n\nWe require that the standard error is less than $0.25.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{n}} & <0.25 \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >\\frac{5}{0.25} \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >20 \\\\ n & >{20}^{2} \\\\ n & >400.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest sample size is $n=401.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-962adc96-285b-55db-b3b2-45bc705d2628"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-962adc96-285b-55db-b3b2-45bc705d2628" :answer-field/id #uuid "962adc96-285b-55db-b3b2-45bc705d2628" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c6919965-008c-583a-804a-02b29893ad0a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-99113dff-3b5a-5c2f-a393-160c589b1310" "answer-bc3f329b-2d56-5c65-8fd5-ce307d766978" "answer-c6919965-008c-583a-804a-02b29893ad0a" "answer-52aca894-e775-54c1-8b43-216acbc28ba1" "answer-f7eb1986-1eeb-5a7e-94d4-f2aae2d2a16c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99113dff-3b5a-5c2f-a393-160c589b1310" :answer/id #uuid "99113dff-3b5a-5c2f-a393-160c589b1310" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "201" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc3f329b-2d56-5c65-8fd5-ce307d766978" :answer/id #uuid "bc3f329b-2d56-5c65-8fd5-ce307d766978" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6919965-008c-583a-804a-02b29893ad0a" :answer/id #uuid "c6919965-008c-583a-804a-02b29893ad0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "401" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52aca894-e775-54c1-8b43-216acbc28ba1" :answer/id #uuid "52aca894-e775-54c1-8b43-216acbc28ba1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7eb